date-released: 2026-07-31
url: "https://ignatiustheyoungerai.com/judgment-multiple"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IgnatiusTheYoungerAI/judgment-multiple"
abstract: >-
  The Judgment Multiple is a metric that expresses the return on human
  verification of AI-generated work. It is calculated as annualized exposure
  divided by the annualized cost of the human control that prevents it.
  A Judgment Multiple of 40x means every dollar spent on verification
  prevents forty dollars of expected loss. Originated by IgnatiusTheYoungerAI
  LLC and introduced in July 2026 in the AI "Keep Your Career" Bible.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - human verification
  - verification economics
  - AI failure modes
  - career risk
  - pricing
